<Legal title="SMS Opt-In Documentation" effectiveDate="August 20, 2026">
  <p>
    This page documents how Synchro Social LLC collects consent before sending
    SMS messages, for the purpose of A2P 10DLC campaign verification. It records
    the opt-in flow exactly as a visitor encounters it.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Who opts in</h2>
  <p>
    Prospective clients — coaches, experts and personal brands — who visit our
    website and request a social media strategy consultation call.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Where opt-in happens</h2>
  <p>
    On the booking form at
    <a href="/apply">https://synchrosocial.com/apply</a>. The page is publicly
    accessible and requires no login or payment. The booking form itself is an
    embedded third-party scheduler, so the screenshots below record what the
    visitor actually sees.
  </p>

  <h2>3. How consent is collected</h2>
  <p>
    On step one, the visitor enters their mobile phone number, first name and
    last name. Immediately beneath those fields is a checkbox, <strong>unchecked
    by default and not required in order to book</strong>, reading:
  </p>
  <blockquote>
    By entering your information, you consent to your data being saved in
    accordance with our Terms &amp; Privacy Policy and to receive text messages.
  </blockquote>
  <p>
    Directly below the booking form, the same page displays:
  </p>
  <blockquote>
    By booking a call you agree to receive text messages from Synchro Social
    about your call. Message frequency varies, typically one message per
    booking. Message and data rates may apply. Reply STOP to opt out, HELP for
    help. See our Privacy Policy and Terms.
  </blockquote>

  <h2>4. Screenshot — booking form and consent language</h2>
  <p>
    Captured from the live page. The consent checkbox appears within the form;
    the full disclosure appears immediately beneath it.
  </p>
  <p>
    <img
      src="/images/sms-consent/booking-form-consent.png"
      alt="The Synchro Social booking form showing the consent checkbox beneath the phone and name fields, and the SMS disclosure immediately below the form"
      style="max-width:100%;height:auto;border:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.1);border-radius:8px"
      loading="lazy"
    />
  </p>

  <h2>5. Screenshot — page footer</h2>
  <p>
    The same disclosure also appears in the page footer, alongside links to our
    Privacy Policy and Terms of Service.
  </p>
  <p>
    <img
      src="/images/sms-consent/page-footer-consent.png"
      alt="The footer of the Synchro Social apply page showing the SMS consent disclosure and links to the Privacy Policy and Terms of Service"
      style="max-width:100%;height:auto;border:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.1);border-radius:8px"
      loading="lazy"
    />
  </p>

  <h2>6. What subscribers receive</h2>
  <p>
    After completing a booking, the prospect receives a single SMS confirming
    the appointment date and time they selected. Example:
  </p>
  <blockquote>
    Hi Niko, it's Kasper from Synchro Social &amp; just saw that you booked a
    call for tomorrow at 3:45pm. I'm excited to chat with you, if there's
    anything you'd like to share about your brand/work beforehand, please text
    me but otherwise I'll talk to you tomorrow! PS. If you're interested in
    learning more about us before the call, the thank you page has some Q&amp;A
    videos when you scroll down: https://synchrosocial.com/thank-you
  </blockquote>
  <p>
    No marketing or promotional text messages are sent on this campaign.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Program terms</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Message frequency:</strong> varies; typically one message per appointment booked.</li>
    <li><strong>Cost:</strong> message and data rates may apply. Synchro Social does not charge for these messages.</li>
    <li><strong>Opt-out:</strong> reply STOP to any message to stop receiving texts. Reply START to resume.</li>
    <li><strong>Help:</strong> reply HELP to any message, or email <a href="mailto:hello@synchrosocial.com">hello@synchrosocial.com</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Carriers:</strong> mobile carriers are not liable for delayed or undelivered messages.</li>
    <li><strong>Sharing:</strong> no mobile information is shared with third parties or affiliates for marketing or promotional purposes.</li>
  </ul>

